(527114, 52057, 8125, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon!  Well deserved, excellent photo - great idea!  Happy New Year!  :-)</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon!  Well deserved, excellent photo - great idea!  Happy New Year!  :-)', '2003-12-31 09:59:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(527128, 51540, 12095, '<td valign="top"><br/>Thanks for everyone''s comments!   The great thing about this site is it challenges us to be creative and to take pictures we wouldn''t normally think of taking.  Even if my picture did not do well in the contest I still would have been happy because I took a picture that I really liked that I would not otherwise have taken.  That said I am THRILLED  at winning my first ribbon!<br/> <br/>I woke up in the middle of the night with the idea.  I got up, got out the camera/tripod and took some test shots in the dresser mirror and thought....hmm....this could work.  The next day, I got out the screw driver, removed the dresser mirror (quite heavy....my wife said YOU BETTER NOT BREAK MY MIRROR) and put it in the back of my pickup.  Drove around town trying to find a good background and finally decided on the fence and hill line.  I thought it would give the picture a feeling of depth and also I could line up the fence and skyline in line with my hand placement.  <br/> <br/>There were several comments about the ring on my hand, yes I could have removed it but then my wife would have KILLED ME!  Actually it was an oversight.  I was too busy worrying about the composition that I didn''t even notice the ring until I uploaded the picture at home. <br/> <br/>Thanks again for the comments, Happy New Year to Everyone!<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for everyone''s comments!   The great thing about this site is it challenges us to be creative and to take pictures we wouldn''t normally think of taking.  Even if my picture did not do well in the contest I still would have been happy because I took a picture that I really liked that I would not otherwise have taken.  That said I am THRILLED  at winning my first ribbon! I woke up in the middle of the night with the idea.  I got up, got out the camera/tripod and took some test shots in the dresser mirror and thought....hmm....this could work.  The next day, I got out the screw driver, removed the dresser mirror (quite heavy....my wife said YOU BETTER NOT BREAK MY MIRROR) and put it in the back of my pickup.  Drove around town trying to find a good background and finally decided on the fence and hill line.  I thought it would give the picture a feeling of depth and also I could line up the fence and skyline in line with my hand placement.   There were several comments about the ring on my hand, yes I could have removed it but then my wife would have KILLED ME!  Actually it was an oversight.  I was too busy worrying about the composition that I didn''t even notice the ring until I uploaded the picture at home.  Thanks again for the comments, Happy New Year to Everyone!  ', '2003-12-31 10:07:14.000000', NULL, 0),
