(530607, 51885, 13136, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by zeuszen:</b></div><hr/><i>The little white specks on the beach (see comments by drgsoell and Natator) are reflections of light from the white of sea shells.<br/> <br/> While I could have easily removed them via adjustments to brightness and contrast, their inclusion here was critical to me, because it added a subtle but distinct metaphorical quality (the suggestion of stars on a dark plane) to the photo, which made for poetry to my senses.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I did not mean to say the specks were bad. I actually likes their inclusion. They helped make the sand look like the night sky. Congrats on your high finish.</td>', 'Originally posted by zeuszen:The little white specks on the beach (see comments by drgsoell and Natator) are reflections of light from the white of sea shells.  While I could have easily removed them via adjustments to brightness and contrast, their inclusion here was critical to me, because it added a subtle but distinct metaphorical quality (the suggestion of stars on a dark plane) to the photo, which made for poetry to my senses.  I did not mean to say the specks were bad. I actually likes their inclusion. They helped make the sand look like the night sky. Congrats on your high finish.', '2004-01-03 14:05:20.000000', NULL, 0),
