(532616, 52116, 9043, '<td valign="top">very difficult subject matter, well done. the DOF and focus is good. There''s a lot going on in this picture. the bags and trolley of belonging''s draw the eye away from the most interesting part of the image. a tight crop of the gentleman would have given a stronger image.<br/>Also i would like to see the image taken from a lower angle. still, a nice shot.</td>', 'very difficult subject matter, well done. the DOF and focus is good. There''s a lot going on in this picture. the bags and trolley of belonging''s draw the eye away from the most interesting part of the image. a tight crop of the gentleman would have given a stronger image.Also i would like to see the image taken from a lower angle. still, a nice shot.', '2004-01-05 15:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(532629, 52010, 5158, '<td valign="top"><b>Content/Composition</b> <br/>The content is of course very simple, but by taking the challenge topic very literally it fits just right. You also did chose a fully symmetric composition, which was a strong, hence good choice. There might be different interesting angle of view to the same subjects, but then it wouldn''t be your image anymore. So you did a great job here.<br/>Also the relation between the pea and the plate was well set by your cropping.<br/>Speaking of cropping: that''s of course one of the most important part in your image. It makes a great balance between the black and white part. Very well done!<br/>Light is also set greatly. I like the variation of bluish greys on the plate and the same subtle variations of green on the pea. Also that any harsh reflections has been avoided has to be noted. Thumb up!<br/>Only the black should be featureless (first I thought it was dust on my screen:)). Of course, pure black (as well as pure white) is one of the  most complicated tasks.<br/> <br/><b>Camera work -technically</b> <br/>Nothing special to mention here: focus is great (not much to focus though) and exposure excellent.<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>Can''t see anything special worth mentioning.<br/> <br/><b>Fits the challenge</b> <br/>Of course it does.<br/> <br/>Good luck for you further submissions.<br/> <br/>Jörg</td>', 'Content/Composition The content is of course very simple, but by taking the challenge topic very literally it fits just right. You also did chose a fully symmetric composition, which was a strong, hence good choice. There might be different interesting angle of view to the same subjects, but then it wouldn''t be your image anymore. So you did a great job here.Also the relation between the pea and the plate was well set by your cropping.Speaking of cropping: that''s of course one of the most important part in your image. It makes a great balance between the black and white part. Very well done!Light is also set greatly. I like the variation of bluish greys on the plate and the same subtle variations of green on the pea. Also that any harsh reflections has been avoided has to be noted. Thumb up!Only the black should be featureless (first I thought it was dust on my screen:)). Of course, pure black (as well as pure white) is one of the  most complicated tasks. Camera work -technically Nothing special to mention here: focus is great (not much to focus though) and exposure excellent. Digital Processing - Technical Can''t see anything special worth mentioning. Fits the challenge Of course it does. Good luck for you further submissions. Jörg', '2004-01-05 15:55:02.000000', NULL, 0),
